  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public Procurement Auctions in S&#xE3;o Paulo: Leveraging Big Data to Improve Performance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Public procurement is one of the core functions of the state, providing key inputs into the delivery of critical public services. From medicines to stationary, governments in developing countries spend a sizable share of their tax revenues on purchases that are determinants of the quality and quantity of final services delivered back to taxpayers. Recent advances in information technology have created a wealth of data that can both unveil key bottlenecks in the purchase systems, and provide an opportunity for governments to improve the performance of public procurement.</narrative>
  </description>
